# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_orm_dsl.py" "ORM-DSL GATE: PASS" "ORM-DSL extractor (Rails Active Record + Laravel Eloquent schema coverage)" "Rails Active Record (create_table :t / alter methods / self.table_name=) and Laravel Eloquent (Schema::create/table / protected \$table) both mint table nodes and alters/queries edges, lighting up the cross-substrate crown jewel for Ruby and PHP repos." "Adds Rails Active Record and Laravel Eloquent schema-DDL extraction to _cg_schema._ORM_PATTERNS so these frameworks mint table nodes (and alters/queries edges) instead of 0. The gap: _ORM_PATTERNS covered Django/SQLAlchemy/JPA + raw SQL but not Rails (create_table :name / db/schema.rb double-quoted / self.table_name= / add_column alter methods) nor Laravel (Schema::create + Schema::table migration DSL / protected \$table Eloquent model property). Without this, Rails and Laravel apps extracted 0 table nodes -> the cross-substrate crown jewel (migration alters T + model queries T with NO import/call edge between them) was invisible. WHAT THIS GATE PROVES (hermetic, no DB, no Postgres, no network): (1) Rails migration DSL: create_table :orders mints table node + alters edge from the db/migrate/ file; alter methods (add_column, add_index) on the same table also mint the table if not yet present; (2) Rails schema.rb: double-quoted create_table \"users\" form (used in db/schema.rb, which is not a migration) mints table nodes; (3) Rails explicit self.table_name = \"legacy_orders\" in a model mints the table + queries edge; (4) Laravel Schema::create('users', ...) and Schema::table('users', ...) in a database/migrations/ file mint the table + alters edges; (5) Laravel protected \$table = 'mention_history' in a model class mints the table + queries edge; (6) CROSS-SUBSTRATE CROWN JEWEL: a Laravel migration (alters page_revisions) and a Laravel model (queries page_revisions) are coupled via the shared table node with CONFIRMED absence of any calls/imports edge between the two files -- exactly what code-only tools miss; (7) never-crash: empty files + binary-ish non-UTF-8 content do not raise; (8) content-free: no file body ever emits (a secret string embedded in a migration body is absent from the full graph string). PRECISION GUARD: patterns are anchored on ORM-specific tokens (create_table keyword / Schema:: namespace / self.table_name property / protected \$table class property) so ordinary Ruby/PHP code that happens to mention a table name in a string literal cannot match. Schema::drop / Schema::dropIfExists are excluded (they do not accept a table-name argument in the capture group). MEASURED on real repos: lobsters (Rails) 0->51 table nodes / 212 alters / 92 queries; BookStack (Laravel) 0->47 table nodes / 130 alters / 7 queries." 20
